{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>They saw.</b> R. Solomon [Rashi] said that in the Ishmaelite language the translation of מן הוא (what is it) is מה הוא, and the one who told him this did not speak accurately, for the translation of מה הוא in the Ishmaelite language is מה הוי, whereas מן הור translates as מי היא (what is it), for in their language it [min] is not applied except to a person, for מן הור is from the root of אשר מנה את מאכלכם (who appointed your food) (Daniel 1:10)." "Said R. Moses the Kohen: We know that there is no before and after in the Torah, for 'and Moses said to them' — yet Moses had already said to them, and similar cases are many. And in this passage: וירם תולעים ויבאש (and it bred worms and stank) (v. 20) — yet it had already stunk. And likewise it is written: ולא הבאיש ורמה לא היתה בו (and it did not stink, and no worm was in it) (v. 24). And Scripture delayed the words of Moses because he needs to elaborate, to say: זה הדבר אשר צוה ה׳ (this is the thing that HaShem commanded)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:35:07.328860297Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}